;; Brood project manifest (ADR-020) — read only by Brood tooling (`brood test`),
;; never by Cargo. It sits ALONGSIDE the Rust workspace and changes nothing about
;; it: this stays a normal Cargo project (crates/, Cargo.toml, std/) that also
;; happens to expose its in-language suite to `brood test`.
;;
;; Convention over configuration: by default source is `src/` and tests are
;; `tests/` (each <name>_test.blsp), but both are overridable here via
;; :source-paths / :test-paths. This repo has no Brood app `src/` — the standard
;; library is embedded (std/*.blsp) and the language itself is Rust (crates/) — so
;; we only point the runner at the in-language tests in `tests/`.
;; `tests/support` is on :source-paths so the conformance runners can
;; `(:use corpus)` — the shared helper for locating the vendored external corpora
;; under tests/corpus/ (see ROADMAP "External conformance corpora"). It is source,
;; not tests: discovery only picks up `*_test.blsp`.
;; `:format-paths` names the trees `nest format` owns beyond source+test. This repo
;; keeps most of its Brood *outside* :source-paths — the standard library is embedded
;; (std/*.blsp, compiled into the binary rather than loaded from a source path), and
;; examples/scripts/stress/breakage are authored but never built from. The formatter
;; walks a whitelist (so it can't rewrite a fetched dep under _deps/), so each of those
;; has to be named here or it would silently stop being formatted.
(project
  :name "brood"
  ;; Must match the Cargo workspace version (crates are `version.workspace = true`).
  ;; Nothing derives one from the other, so `version_matches_cargo` in
  ;; crates/lisp/tests/manifest_version.rs asserts they agree — this said 0.1.0 for
  ;; twelve releases before that test existed.
  :version "0.18.1"
  :source-paths ["tests/support"]
  :test-paths ["tests"]
  :format-paths ["std" "examples" "scripts" "stress" "breakage"])
; override; e.g. :source-paths ["lib"] for a real app
